From c799839e764049504a022a5dc51051fbdd9ec3d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:47:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/92] moe-stream : where decode loads come from and how long
 they take (SiegeLadder M12), the late drop, and the drop masks on the remap's
 host split - counters: every slot remembers its load's source (the host tier
 or the drive, from l2::has, which counts and marks nothing) and when it was
 reserved; print_stats splits the staged experts by source (ready / still
 loading / not asked for), the decode waits by what was in flight when they
 began (a drive read of the call's own, drive reads staged ahead only,
 host-tier copies only: calls and seconds), and prints delivery times
 (reservation to the last copy enqueued) and the time left once a call waited,
 as histograms per class; the remap halves time their wait for mgr->mtx (G21).
 SiegeLadder runs.md 4.53-4.54: with runahead every remaining wait is the
 drive, 70% of it stages ahead from the drive that arrive late (2.5-2.6 ms
 against a lead of ~1.9), 30% misses runahead did not predict; the lock costs
 0.001-0.002 ms per call. LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_DROP_LATE=1 (lossy, next to the
 plain drop rule and runahead): at the wait the call waits for its heavy
 experts only and drops the light ones still loading, whose loads go on for
 later calls - KL 0.011-0.016, +1..+4% over runahead, so not for the fast
 preset. The drop rule's mask (drop_mask, and exact_mask next to runahead) is
 expanded right after its remap: left to the final weighting's expansion it
 came after the expert GEMMs in node order, a host split of its own and one
 more card-host-card hand-off per layer; drop 0.14 14.06 -> 14.44 tok/s, and
 the deterministic DROP_VRAM_ONLY=3 gives the same logits in both orders (PPL,
 KL, max KLD, top-1, 92 633 drops identical);
 LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MASK_LATE_SPLIT=1 keeps the old order for A/B

